From beff09c3acfa3dd67f535efce7e13eddd82fb32b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lolzen <funer@gmx.at>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:29:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] session: Log out through logind without systemd --user

Switching sessions logged out by stopping graphical-session.target in the
user's systemd instance. Without a user service manager, as on runit
systems, steamos-manager runs inside the login session it serves, so it
now asks logind to terminate that session, found by its own PID. As this
ends steamos-manager too, the session is terminated a moment after the
call has returned, so the caller still gets its reply; with systemd the
stop of the target is only queued as well. systemd systems are unchanged.
---
